## Assessment of Refinement Suggestions

### Suggestions Worth Adopting

| # | Suggestion | Verdict |
|---|-----------|---------|
| 3 | Rename `SymbolInfo.jsdoc` → `rawDocumentation` | ✅ Good — language-agnostic naming |
| 7 | Lazy registration for `LanguageAnalyzerRegistry` | ✅ Good — avoids loading Python analyzer when not needed |
| 12 | Use lockfiles as primary source for `DependencyMapper` | ✅ Good — more accurate versions |
| 13 | `SemanticAnnotator` LLM circuit breaker | ✅ Good — critical for resilience |
| 15 | `PromptBudgetEnforcer` integration | ✅ **Essential** — must be added |
| 16 | `CrossRefLinker` symbol disambiguation | ✅ Good — needs concrete strategy |
| 17 | `DocValidator` secret scanning patterns | ✅ Good — concrete implementation needed |
| 20 | Register as `doc:generate` tool in `ToolRegistry` | ✅ **Excellent idea** — enables invocation from general-coding tasks |
| 25 | Dependency-cruiser boundary rule for `doc-generator/` | ✅ **Essential** — must be added to `.dependency-cruiser.js` |

### Suggestions That Are Overengineered or Premature

| # | Suggestion | Verdict |
|---|-----------|---------|
| 2 | Rename `jsdoc` field | ⚠️ Premature — Phase 1 is TypeScript-only; rename when Python support matures |
| 4 | Add `analyzeDirectory()` to `ILanguageAnalyzer` | ⚠️ Overengineered — batch analysis can be done by the orchestrator calling `analyzeFile()` in parallel |
| 6 | Add `'doc-generation'` as third `taskMode` | ⚠️ Overengineered — doc generation can run as a CLI command without entering the `CognitiveEngine` task pipeline. Adding a third mode increases routing complexity for a feature that doesn't need the full agent task lifecycle |
| 9 | Use Python `ast` via child process | ⚠️ Fragile — spawning Python as a child process creates a runtime dependency. Regex-based analysis with lower confidence scores is the right tradeoff for Phase 1 |
| 22 | Add `doc-generator` metrics to `AnomalyDetector` | ⚠️ Premature — add after the feature is stable, not during initial implementation |

